-# Digital Service Orchestra (DSO) — CI Skip
-#
-# Companion to ci.yml that fires ONLY for docs-only PRs (paths matching
-# **/*.md). Each job emits a check-context with the SAME `name:` as its
-# counterpart in ci.yml, so branch-protection required checks are satisfied
-# without running the heavy gates.
-#
-# Why this exists: ci.yml uses `paths-ignore: '**/*.md'`, which causes its
-# required checks to remain "expected" forever on docs-only PRs and blocks
-# merge. This pattern is GitHub's documented workaround.
-#
-# Sync invariant: the set of `name:` fields below MUST equal
-#   (ci.yml jobs) ∩ (.github/required-checks.txt)
-# Enforced by plugins/dso/scripts/onboarding/validate-ci-skip-parity.sh,
-# wired into ci.yml's `validate-required-checks` job.
-
-name: CI Skip
-
-on:
-  pull_request:
-    branches:
-      - main
-    paths:
-      - '**/*.md'
-
-concurrency:
-  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}
-  cancel-in-progress: true
-
-jobs:
-  actionlint:
-    name: Actionlint
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    timeout-minutes: 1
-    steps:
-      - run: echo "Skipped — docs-only PR"
-
-  shellcheck:
-    name: ShellCheck
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    timeout-minutes: 1
-    steps:
-      - run: echo "Skipped — docs-only PR"
-
-  lint-python:
